{"_id":"68df9647166b018f83df8601","roadmapSlug":"css","nodeId":"SNcVcjcvtph3W7KTx1N-v","description":"# Transitions\n\nTransitions in CSS allow you to smoothly change property values over a specified duration. Instead of an abrupt change, a transition creates a gradual effect when a CSS property changes, such as when hovering over an element or when a class is added or removed. This adds visual polish and improves the user experience by making interactions feel more fluid and responsive.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"CSS transitions","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_transitions","_id":"6a67293033d15c831021451f"},{"type":"article","title":"Using CSS transitions","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_transitions/Using_CSS_transitions","_id":"6a67293033d15c8310214520"},{"type":"video","title":"Animating with CSS Transitions - A look at the transition properties","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Nloq6uzF8RQ","_id":"6a67293033d15c8310214521"}],"createdAt":"2025-10-03T09:24:23.152Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-27T09:47:28.129Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a22adddac1c5fa9928ab3ab","title":"CSS Fundamentals","slug":"css","description":"Style, lay out, and debug real pages without fighting the cascade.","lessonIds":["6a15d62fac1c5fa9928a3fb6","6a15e1b0ac1c5fa9928a403f","6a16f11aac1c5fa9928a7c14","6a19dcdfac1c5fa9928a84a5","6a19e79cac1c5fa9928a8571","6a19f85cac1c5fa9928a8654","6a1d7a23ac1c5fa9928a8b4e","6a1dd2daac1c5fa9928a9884","6a1ecf18ac1c5fa9928a9a81","6a1f3245ac1c5fa9928a9cdd","6a20aa64ac1c5fa9928aa44a","6a20ba69ac1c5fa9928aa755","6a20c105ac1c5fa9928aa818","6a20c2e5ac1c5fa9928aa847","6a20c490ac1c5fa9928aa871","6a20c5adac1c5fa9928aa884","6a20c6a5ac1c5fa9928aa897","6a20c7c5ac1c5fa9928aa8aa","6a20ca2fac1c5fa9928aa8d0","6a20cb82ac1c5fa9928aa8e3"],"projectIds":["68b7185fffbff9183d772aed","68b7185fffbff9183d772aee","68b7185fffbff9183d772af0","68b7185fffbff9183d772af6","6a26960eac1c5fa9928acb63","6a26b431ac1c5fa9928acefa"],